    "['radius-server accounting [parameter1] [parameter2] weight [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'radius-server host 192.168.7.249 auth-port 1645 acct-port 1646 key %^%#`E)v.Q@BHVzxxZ;ij{>&_M0!TGP7YRA@8a7mq<\\\\/%^%#', 'parent_command': ['aaa group server radius rd4'], 'root': 'aaa group server radius rd4', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Huawei `radius-server accounting` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nradius-server host 192.168.7.249 auth-port 1645 acct-port 1646 key %^%#`E)v.Q@BHVzxxZ;ij{>&_M0!TGP7YRA@8a7mq<\\\\/%^%#\\n##\\n\\nNotes about the translation:\\n1. Cisco combines both authentication and accounting server configuration in one command\\n2. The shared key is preserved from the original configuration (though in practice it should be properly encrypted in Cisco)\\n3. The weight parameter isn't directly translatable as Cisco handles RADIUS server selection differently\\n4. The auth-port and acct-port values are kept as per the original (1645/1646)\\n5. The authentication port (1645) is added though it wasn't in the original command being translated, as Cisco requires both ports in one command\", 'trans_template': 'radius-server host 192.168.7.249 auth-port 1645 acct-port 1646 key %^%#`E)v.Q@BHVzxxZ;ij{>&_M0!TGP7YRA@8a7mq<\\\\/%^%#'}]]": 1,
