    "['radius-server type [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'radius-server vsa send accounting', 'parent_command': ['aaa group server radius rd4'], 'root': 'aaa group server radius rd4', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for `radius-server type plus11`:\\n\\n##\\nradius-server vsa send accounting\\nradius-server vsa send authentication\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Huawei, `radius-server type plus11` enables support for RADIUS vendor-specific attributes (VSAs) following the \"plus11\" format (similar to Cisco\\'s VSA implementation).\\n- In Cisco, this is achieved by enabling VSA support for both accounting and authentication separately.\\n- The Cisco commands ensure that vendor-specific attributes are included in RADIUS messages, which is the functional equivalent of Huawei\\'s \"plus11\" type.', 'trans_template': 'radius-server vsa send accounting'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'radius-server vsa send authentication', 'parent_command': ['aaa group server radius rd4'], 'root': 'aaa group server radius rd4', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for `radius-server type plus11`:\\n\\n##\\nradius-server vsa send accounting\\nradius-server vsa send authentication\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Huawei, `radius-server type plus11` enables support for RADIUS vendor-specific attributes (VSAs) following the \"plus11\" format (similar to Cisco\\'s VSA implementation).\\n- In Cisco, this is achieved by enabling VSA support for both accounting and authentication separately.\\n- The Cisco commands ensure that vendor-specific attributes are included in RADIUS messages, which is the functional equivalent of Huawei\\'s \"plus11\" type.', 'trans_template': 'radius-server vsa send authentication'}]]": 1,
    "['radius-server traffic-unit [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'radius-server vsa send traffic-unit kbytes', 'parent_command': ['aaa group server radius rd4'], 'root': 'aaa group server radius rd4', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nradius-server vsa send traffic-unit kbytes\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei command `radius-server traffic-unit kbyte` configures the unit for traffic statistics to be sent to the RADIUS server as kilobytes.\\n- The Cisco equivalent is `radius-server vsa send traffic-unit kbytes`, which specifies that traffic accounting should be reported in kilobytes using Vendor-Specific Attributes (VSA).\\n- Note that Cisco uses the plural \"kbytes\" while Huawei uses \"kbyte\".', 'trans_template': 'radius-server vsa send traffic-unit kbytes'}]]": 1,
